      "text": [
        "936 - لِقَوْلِ أَبِي جَعْفَرٍ اَلثَّانِي عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ: «لاَ بَأْسَ أَنْ يَتَكَلَّمَ اَلرَّجُلُ فِي صَلاَةِ اَلْفَرِيضَةِ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ يُنَاجِي بِهِ رَبَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.936 - The saying of Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Jawad (as):\n\"There is no harm if a person speaks in the obligatory prayer with anything by which he converses with his Lord (azj), Mighty and Majestic.\""
        ]
      }
